controls.py: refuse an unknown check() stage

check(E, F, stage) treated every stage other than 'E' as stage 1, so a
mistyped stage silently dropped the result-note requirement of S4 and R.
check() now raises on any stage outside ('E', 'S1'), and the end-to-end
self-test gains a case requiring that refusal (21 cases). The
preregistration pins the new controls.py blob.

